content.text:
To turn hibernation off, set a static `options` property with `hibernate: false` on your Agent class:

```ts
import { Agent } from "agents";

export class AlwaysOnAgent extends Agent<Env> {
  static options = { hibernate: false };
}
```

Hibernation is on by default. With it on, the agent's Durable Object can be taken out of memory while idle, and the WebSocket connections stay open. With it off, the instance stays in memory as long as a connection is open. That keeps in-memory state between messages, but you pay for the whole time it's held in memory. Unless you really need that in-memory state, it's usually better to leave hibernation on and save state with `this.setState` or SQL.

The code is from the Agents WebSockets docs page, which says "Hibernation is enabled by default. To disable:" right before this example.

Sources:
- [Cloudflare Agents – WebSockets](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/runtime/communication/websockets/)
- [Cloudflare Agents API reference](https://developers.cloudflare.com/agents/runtime/agents-api/index.md)

